{"name":"Winning Ticket","hex":"#636653","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"winning","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of win"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["That constitutes a win.","That leads to success."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/winning"},{"term":"ticket","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small document that acts as proof of something, often thereby granting the holder some ability.\nA pass entitling the holder to admission to a show, concert, sporting event, etc.","A pass entitling the holder to admission to a show, concert, sporting event, etc."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To issue someone a ticket, as for travel or for a violation of a local or traffic law.","To mark with a ticket."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ticket"}],"entries":[{"title":"Winning Ticket","blocks":[{"text":"Winning Ticket was a Japanese Thoroughbred racehorse and stud. He is best known for winning the 1993 Tōkyō Yūshun. Winning Ticket was part of the \"BNW\" trio along with Biwa Hayahide and Narita Taishin that were rivals challenging for the Japanese Triple Crown. Winning Ticket was also a moderately successful sire after his racing career."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Winning_Ticket_20070422P1.jpg/330px-Winning_Ticket_20070422P1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Winning_Ticket"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Winning_Ticket_2013.jpg/500px-Winning_Ticket_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Winning_Ticket_2013.jpg/1280px-Winning_Ticket_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Winning_Ticket